From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:51:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Say when an animation's or transition's output next
 changes

An embedder ticks CSS animations by resolving styles again while any
animation or transition needs ticks, which in practice is every frame.
A `steps()` easing changes its output only at its steps, and an
animation or transition in its delay not before it starts, so most of
those frames resolve to the same style.

Add `next_change(now)` to `Animation`, `Transition` and
`ElementAnimationSet`: when the output may next change, at or after
`now`. `None` while paused, finished or canceled; the start while in a
delay; for a `steps()` easing, the next jump, the end of its keyframe
segment or the end of the iteration, whichever is first (per property,
with the keyframe and direction the value is computed from); `now`
while an easing moves continuously, or when the animation is due to
iterate or finish. The keyframe lookup `get_property_declaration_at_time`
does is factored out into `keyframes_around` so both use it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
